From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arjan van de Ven <arjan.van.de.ven@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Nov 2021 17:38:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mm: size PCP batches by zone and total memory

Fold the 6.18 batch divisor into the zone shifts and size caps. Use
1/8192 of the zone, capped at 256 KiB, above 2032 MiB of RAM. At or
below 2032 MiB use 1/4096, raising the cap to 512 KiB from 640 MiB.
Keep the minimum and power-of-two rounding; do not set a PCP high watermark.
---
--- a/mm/page_alloc.c
+++ b/mm/page_alloc.c
@@ -6162,17 +6162,19 @@ void __ref build_all_zonelists(pg_data_t
 
 static int zone_batchsize(struct zone *zone)
 {
 #ifdef CONFIG_MMU
+	unsigned long mem_mb = totalram_pages() / (SZ_1M / PAGE_SIZE);
 	int batch;
 
-	/*
-	 * The number of pages to batch allocate is either ~0.025%
-	 * of the zone or 256KB, whichever is smaller. The batch
-	 * size is striking a balance between allocation latency
-	 * and zone lock contention.
-	 */
-	batch = min(zone_managed_pages(zone) >> 12, SZ_256K / PAGE_SIZE);
+	/* Fold the 6.18 final division by four into the shifts and caps. */
+	if (mem_mb <= 2032) {
+		unsigned long cap = mem_mb >= 640 ? SZ_512K : SZ_256K;
+
+		batch = min(zone_managed_pages(zone) >> 12, cap / PAGE_SIZE);
+	} else {
+		batch = min(zone_managed_pages(zone) >> 13, SZ_256K / PAGE_SIZE);
+	}
 	if (batch <= 1)
 		return 1;
 
 	/*
